    <dl class="kv">
      <dt>Thesis title</dt>
      <dd>Proper Tail Calls From First‑Class Continuations in JavaScript (<a href="/assets/docs/caner_bsc_thesis.pdf"><strong>PDF</strong></a>)</dd>
      <dt>Supervisors</dt>
      <dd>Chris Stephenson, Shriram Krishnamurthi, Alpaslan Parlakçı, Matthew Edwards</dd>
      <dt>Abstract</dt>
      <dd>This thesis demonstrates that proper tail‑call behaviour in JavaScript is possible without modifying the interpreter. It is based on the paper “Continuations from Generalized Stack Inspection” (Pettyjohn et al.), which presents a program transformation for obtaining first‑class continuations from exception‑handling mechanisms. My work extends their technique to achieve tail‑call optimized computation without touching the interpreter.</dd>
    </dl>
